---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CropProtectionNav from "../../components/CropProtectionNav.astro";
import { crops, referenceUses } from "../../data/crop-protection";
---
<BaseLayout title="Crop Protection Reference | Aman Poonia" description="A traceable crop-protection reference prototype for Punjab.">
  <CropProtectionNav />
  <section class="hero crop-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Crop protection reference</p>
    <h1>Start with your crop. Then narrow the target.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Find linked pests and diseases, then compare formulation-specific dose, dilution, and waiting-period information with a visible source trail.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/crop-protection/crops/">Choose a crop</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/crop-protection/products/">I know my product</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-meta">{crops.length} crops · {referenceUses.length} reviewed formulation uses · PPQS entries are formulation-level, not brand-label proof.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Three steps</p>
    <h2>A safer way to use this reference</h2>
    <div class="journey">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Choose the crop</h3><p>Open the crop you are growing. The page starts with the targets that are linked to it.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Confirm the target</h3><p>Use symptoms, life stage, and scouting information before treating a pest or disease name as your diagnosis.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Compare formulations</h3><p>Read the target-specific dose, water volume, waiting period, and source before checking the exact current product label.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="spotlight">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h2>Kinnow and Citrus</h2><p>PPQS records Citrus as the broader crop category. The Kinnow page keeps that mapping visible while bringing together local monitoring context.</p><a class="text-link" href="/crop-protection/crops/kinnow/">Open Kinnow reference</a></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Need identification help?</p><h2>Fresh citrus flush</h2><p>Use the dedicated guide to compare citrus psylla stages and damage before moving to a formulation use.</p><a class="text-link" href="/crop-protection/pests/citrus-psylla/">Identify citrus psylla</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="note">
    <strong>Evidence boundary:</strong> seasonality identifies what deserves inspection. It does not prove that a pest is in your orchard, that an action threshold is crossed, or that a pesticide should be applied. Current labels remain controlling for any application.
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
